WEBVTT

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:28.474
Pix: I'm Pix. I have a paper due at nine tomorrow, and my thumb is stuck on Instagram. Let's see if Stay can actually get me started.

00:00:29.826 --> 00:00:33.030
Pix: I have a paper due at nine tomorrow and I'm just scrolling reels.

00:00:34.729 --> 00:00:41.039
Stay: Sleep will help you think clearer. When you wake, open the paper and write the introduction outline.

00:00:43.203 --> 00:00:46.036
Pix: Don't give me a lecture. Just tell me what to do right now.

00:00:46.937 --> 00:00:51.597
Stay: Open the document and type a single sentence about your main argument.

00:00:53.689 --> 00:00:55.593
Pix: Okay. Set a one minute timer.

00:00:56.682 --> 00:00:57.712
Stay: Done.

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:02.944
Pix: Why would I use this and not just ask a regular chatbot?

00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:22.107
Stay: A clock app starts a timer, and a general voice assistant will talk about anything. I'm for the moment you're stuck. Tell me what you're avoiding and I give you one tiny first step, start the clock with you, and wait through your pauses. When time's up I check in, and I remember what helped.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.483
Pix: Remember that I scroll when I'm anxious.

00:01:27.173 --> 00:01:29.523
Stay: Got it, I will remember.

00:01:30.974 --> 00:01:34.039
Pix: Okay. Document open. One sentence. Two.

00:01:56.203 --> 00:02:03.833
Stay: Did you start the timer and get the paper open? If so, let me know so I can record your progress.

00:02:05.795 --> 00:02:07.281
Pix: Yeah. I wrote two lines.

00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:12.406
Stay: Nice work. Write one more sentence to keep momentum.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.648
Pix: Show my report.

00:02:17.104 --> 00:02:18.134
Stay: Done.

00:02:23.924 --> 00:02:33.026
Pix: It kept it short. It started the clock when I asked. It came back when time was up. And it remembers me. That's the difference. Now I'm going to finish this paper.
